{
  "id": "ep072",
  "duration": 50.098,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.747,
      "text": "A monster solar storm missed erasing our modern world by nine days.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Magnificent CME Erupts on the Sun - August 31.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magnificent_CME_Erupts_on_the_Sun_-_August_31.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.733,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.747,
      "end": 11.441,
      "text": "In July 2012, the Sun launched a massive eruption matching the strongest storm ever recorded.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Sun Sends Two CMEs Toward Mercury (8681308268).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center from Greenbelt, MD, USA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Sun_Sends_Two_CMEs_Toward_Mercury_(8681308268).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.733,
          "end": 11.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.441,
      "end": 18.111,
      "text": "This blast traveled over two thousand kilometers per second, four times faster than a typical storm.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Storms From the Sun (6819077978).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center from Greenbelt, MD, USA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Storms_From_the_Sun_(6819077978).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.433,
          "end": 18.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.111,
      "end": 24.732,
      "text": "It achieved this record speed because another eruption four days earlier had cleared its cosmic path.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Coronal Mass Ejection Headed for Earth? (4860149819).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center from Greenbelt, MD, USA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coronal_Mass_Ejection_Headed_for_Earth%3F_(4860149819).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.1,
          "end": 24.733,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.732,
      "end": 31.076,
      "text": "A direct hit would have crippled global power grids and water pumps, costing over two trillion dollars.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.733,
          "end": 31.067,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.076,
      "end": 37.201,
      "text": "Instead, NASA's STEREO-A spacecraft took the hit and survived to show us what we missed.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist rendering of STEREO-A (PIA18171).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/GSFC",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist_rendering_of_STEREO-A_(PIA18171).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.067,
          "end": 37.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.201,
      "end": 43.971,
      "text": "Physicist Pete Riley calculated a twelve percent chance a similar storm strikes Earth every decade.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.2,
          "end": 43.967,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.971,
      "end": 49.748,
      "text": "We survived only because the erupting region of the Sun was no longer pointed directly at us.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Magnificent CME Erupts on the Sun - August 31.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magnificent_CME_Erupts_on_the_Sun_-_August_31.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.967,
          "end": 50.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
